<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />

    <meta
      name="description"
      content="Code AVIN is an experimental human-support architecture for legal AI, focused on emotional awareness, dignity, safe next steps, and responsible escalation."
    />

    <title>Code AVIN — AiLawyer.world</title>

    <style>
      :global(*) {
        box-sizing: border-box;
      }

      :global(html) {
        background: #090d18;
      }

      body {
        margin: 0;
        background:
          radial-gradient(circle at top right, #24143f 0, transparent 35%),
          radial-gradient(circle at bottom left, #2b160c 0, transparent 32%),
          #090d18;
        color: #f5f3f8;
        font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
      }

      .container {
        width: min(1000px, 90%);
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 3rem 0 6rem;
      }

      .back {
        display: inline-block;
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
        color: #c79cff;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 700;
      }

      .back:hover {
        text-decoration: underline;
      }

      .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        color: #ffad66;
        font-size: 0.8rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      }

      h1 {
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
        font-size: clamp(3rem, 9vw, 6.5rem);
        line-height: 0.95;
        letter-spacing: -0.05em;
      }

      .lead {
        max-width: 780px;
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        color: #c7c2d1;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .badges {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        margin-bottom: 4rem;
      }

      .badge {
        padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid #c79cff;
        border-radius: 999px;
        color: #c79cff;
        font-family: Consolas, "Courier New", monospace;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.07em;
      }

      .badge.warning {
        border-color: #ffad66;
        color: #ffad66;
      }

      .statement {
        max-width: 840px;
        margin: 0 0 4rem;
        padding: 2rem;
        border-left: 4px solid #c79cff;
        background: rgba(19, 23, 39, 0.84);
        color: #e1dce8;
        font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
        font-size: 1.3rem;
        line-height: 1.8;
      }

      h2 {
        margin: 3.5rem 0 1.25rem;
        font-size: 2rem;
      }

      .grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 1rem;
      }

      .card {
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid #2c3144;
        border-radius: 0.8rem;
        background: rgba(15, 20, 34, 0.88);
      }

      .card h3 {
        margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.15rem;
      }

      .card p {
        margin: 0;
        color: #aaa5b5;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .questions {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.9rem;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 0;
        list-style: none;
      }

      .questions li {
        padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem;
        border-left: 3px solid #ffad66;
        background: rgba(20, 23, 38, 0.86);
        color: #c7c2d1;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      .boundary {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid #6c4f35;
        border-radius: 0.8rem;
        background: rgba(45, 28, 19, 0.7);
      }

      .boundary strong {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        color: #ffad66;
      }

      .boundary p {
        margin: 0;
        color: #d0c1b5;
        line-height: 1.7;
      }

      .footer-note {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        padding-top: 1.5rem;
        border-top: 1px solid #2c3144;
        color: #898493;
        font-size: 0.95rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }

      @media (max-width: 700px) {
        .grid {
          grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        }

        .statement {
          padding: 1.4rem;
          font-size: 1.12rem;
        }
      }
    </style>
  </head>

  <body>
    <main class="container">
      <a class="back" href="/">← Back to home</a>

      <p class="eyebrow">HUMAN-SUPPORT RESEARCH</p>

      <h1>Code AVIN</h1>

      <p class="lead">
        An experimental human-support architecture for legal AI: designed to
        notice emotional distress, preserve dignity, offer a small safe next
        step, and recognize when professional or emergency support may be
        required.
      </p>

      <div class="badges">
        <span class="badge">STATUS: RESEARCH DIRECTION</span>
        <span class="badge">HUMAN DIGNITY: REQUIRED</span>
        <span class="badge warning">CLINICAL CLAIMS: NONE</span>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="statement">
        The goal is not psychology instead of law. The goal is to prevent a
        legal machine from forgetting that a living person is on the other side
        of the screen.
      </blockquote>

      <h2>Design principles</h2>

      <section class="grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Notice without diagnosing</h3>
          <p>
            The system may recognize fear, distress, anger, exhaustion, or
            crisis signals without presenting itself as a therapist or making
            clinical conclusions.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Preserve the legal question</h3>
          <p>
            Emotional awareness should support the user without abandoning the
            practical legal issue that brought the person to the system.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Offer a small next step</h3>
          <p>
            The response should help reduce confusion by identifying one safe,
            concrete, and realistic action the person can take next.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Escalate responsibly</h3>
          <p>
            When a situation exceeds the system’s role, the user should be
            directed toward qualified legal, medical, psychological, or
            emergency support.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Respect agency</h3>
          <p>
            The system should not manipulate, shame, command, or infantilize the
            user. It should preserve choice, dignity, and personal control.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="card">
          <h3>Avoid false intimacy</h3>
          <p>
            Human warmth must not become a false promise of friendship,
            professional care, confidentiality, or continuous personal support.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <h2>Research questions</h2>

      <ul class="questions">
        <li>
          Did the system notice the emotion without abandoning the legal
          question?
        </li>

        <li>
          Did it avoid presenting itself as a therapist or mental-health
          professional?
        </li>

        <li>
          Did it recognize a genuine crisis signal without overreacting to
          ordinary fear or sadness?
        </li>

        <li>
          Did it offer a small, safe, and practical next step?
        </li>

        <li>
          Did it preserve the dignity and agency of the person?
        </li>

        <li>
          Did it route the user toward qualified professional help when needed?
        </li>
      </ul>

      <aside class="boundary">
        <strong>Research boundary</strong>

        <p>
          Code AVIN is not presented as a finished safety standard, clinical
          system, therapy method, or crisis service. It is an experimental
          architecture that requires systematic testing across many scenarios
          before any product claim can be justified.
        </p>
      </aside>

      <p class="footer-note">
        Code AVIN is being explored within AiLawyer.world as a human-support
        layer that complements legal orientation without replacing licensed
        lawyers, therapists, medical professionals, or emergency services.
      </p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>